  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="0107-f35b-5928-678b" name="Harappan Indian (AoA2) - List Notes" publicationId="fcb9-17be-94c2-bcfc" hidden="false">
      <description>ARMIES OF ANTIQUITY v2 #108 (unofficial, Martin Gibbins). The civilisation of the Indus region in India was a contemporary of, and traded with, Sumer. While the list is largely based on a few archaeological finds and much extrapolation, it provides an interesting alternative early army. The civilisation withered after several crucial rivers changed course, depriving the area of irrigation; the vacuum was filled by the arrival of the Aryans. 

ARMY COMPOSITION:
[Harappan Indian]
  Allies and Mercenaries: up to 25%
  Characters: up to 25%
  Infantry: at least 25%
  Characters: up to 25% Infantry: At least 25% Elephants: 0-1 Allies &amp; Mercenaries: up to 25%</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
